{
  "about": "Python packages the runtime for KiCad's own plugins can load when a plugin imports them. scripts/build-python.mjs downloads them into static/dist/pyodide and checks every file's SHA-256: 'pyodide' names packages of the Pyodide distribution (compiled for WebAssembly; their dependencies come along), 'pypi' names pure Python wheels taken from PyPI at a pinned version and hash. An entry with 'source' is a package PyPI has only as a source archive: its listed modules are taken from the archive (checked against 'sha256') and packed as a wheel by the build.",
